    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld §341-a, amd §§3217-a & 4324, Ins L (as proposed in S.4620-C & A.5411-D); amd §4408, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Insurance Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S836\n\nSPONSOR: BRESLIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the insurance law and the public health law, in relation\nto patient prescription pricing transparency; and to repeal certain\nprovisions of the insurance law related thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2022,\nc., to clarify provisions relating to patient prescription pricing tran-\nsparency\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill requires plans to give real-time data on cost-sharing and\ncoverage to consumers at the point of prescribing. The changes exempt\nthe Medicaid program from this requirement because of a capability\nissue; and make technical amendments.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter of the Laws of 2022. S.4620C and A.5411D\nboth passed the Senate and Assembly in May 2022.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2022 amending the insurance law relating to\nenacting the \"patient Rx information and choice expansion act\", as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S. 4620-C and A. 5411-D, takes\neffect.\n",
